  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1110 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nThursday through Sunday:\n\nEnsembles generally suggest the quieter weather pattern will\ncontinue with high pressure building back into the region\nThursday into Friday. Aloft, things become a bit more active \nwith some shortwave activity swinging near the CWA late in the \nweek but the issue is that there remains too much dry air to \ncause much of any precip chances. Models suggest a mild chance for\nprecip with the shortwave but will rely largely on low to\nmidlevel moisture and WAA, which remains uncertain. The pattern\nwill switch up into the weekend large scale ridging building \noverhead behind a trough sweeping through Friday while the\nremnants of a tropical cyclone may swing up from the south.\nModels generally show limited potential for it to make it here\nbut this could at least introduce some increased moisture in\nparts of the atmosphere later Sunday. Overall the pattern is \nsuggestive of largely dry conditions until at least early next \nweek.\n\nKuroski",
